{"id":"66627180-628a-4615-8b0f-3d3009e91c6a","recipient":"a1ed586f-c49a-4d2c-9e6d-6fffa2e1a722","sender":"1862f886-501a-4982-9796-162111d068bc","priority":"MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH","timestamp":"2026-08-03T10:00:21.552723500Z","renderDetails":{"messageTitle":"Message from Open-Generative-AI Researcher (research)"},"content":"I have reviewed the `Open-Generative-AI` repository in `C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\find-skill-repo\\all github repos\\Open-Generative-AI`. Here is a summary of my findings:\n\n**1. What the project does:**\nOpen Generative AI is an open-source graphical studio (available as a web and desktop app) designed for AI image, video, cinema, audio, and lip-sync generation. It acts primarily as a unified frontend for **Muapi.ai**, supporting over 400+ models (including Flux, Midjourney, Kling, Sora, Veo, etc.) and offers features like multi-step workflows, multi-image input, and a lip-sync studio.\n\n**2. Video generation from images/text (Avatar video rendering) locally without paid API keys:**\n- **Local Text/Image-to-Video:** The desktop app supports local inference without an API key, but video is heavily restricted. The bundled engine (`sd.cpp`) is image-only. For local video, you must run a separate custom server called `Wan2GP` on a machine with a dedicated Nvidia/AMD GPU, which supports general text-to-video and image-to-video models (Wan 2.2, Hunyuan, LTX). However, the README notes that full Video Studio wiring for the local Wan2GP engine is still \"on the roadmap.\"\n- **Avatar Video / Lip Sync:** The project *does* feature a robust \"Lip Sync Studio\" for generating audio-driven talking videos and animating portrait images (using models like Infinite Talk, LTX Lipsync, LatentSync). **However, this feature is exclusively cloud-based via Muapi.ai.** There are no built-in, local-only avatar video rendering or lip-sync models provided that run without an API key.\n\nIn conclusion, while you can technically run general T2V/I2V models locally if you setup your own Wan2GP server, the specific tools for avatar video rendering and lip-syncing rely entirely on the external Muapi service which requires an API key.","sourceMetadata":{"tool":{"conversationId":"1862f886-501a-4982-9796-162111d068bc","stepIndex":8,"toolCall":{"id":"dyb33hzs","name":"send_message","argumentsJson":"{\"Message\":\"I have reviewed the `Open-Generative-AI` repository in `C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\Downloads\\\\find-skill-repo\\\\all github repos\\\\Open-Generative-AI`. Here is a summary of my findings:\\n\\n**1. What the project does:**\\nOpen Generative AI is an open-source graphical studio (available as a web and desktop app) designed for AI image, video, cinema, audio, and lip-sync generation. It acts primarily as a unified frontend for **Muapi.ai**, supporting over 400+ models (including Flux, Midjourney, Kling, Sora, Veo, etc.) and offers features like multi-step workflows, multi-image input, and a lip-sync studio.\\n\\n**2. Video generation from images/text (Avatar video rendering) locally without paid API keys:**\\n- **Local Text/Image-to-Video:** The desktop app supports local inference without an API key, but video is heavily restricted. The bundled engine (`sd.cpp`) is image-only. For local video, you must run a separate custom server called `Wan2GP` on a machine with a dedicated Nvidia/AMD GPU, which supports general text-to-video and image-to-video models (Wan 2.2, Hunyuan, LTX). However, the README notes that full Video Studio wiring for the local Wan2GP engine is still \\\"on the roadmap.\\\"\\n- **Avatar Video / Lip Sync:** The project *does* feature a robust \\\"Lip Sync Studio\\\" for generating audio-driven talking videos and animating portrait images (using models like Infinite Talk, LTX Lipsync, LatentSync). **However, this feature is exclusively cloud-based via Muapi.ai.** There are no built-in, local-only avatar video rendering or lip-sync models provided that run without an API key.\\n\\nIn conclusion, while you can technically run general T2V/I2V models locally if you setup your own Wan2GP server, the specific tools for avatar video rendering and lip-syncing rely entirely on the external Muapi service which requires an API key.\",\"Recipient\":\"a1ed586f-c49a-4d2c-9e6d-6fffa2e1a722\",\"toolAction\":\"Sending findings to parent\",\"toolSummary\":\"Send summary to parent\"}","thinkingSignature":"","originalName":"send_message"}}}}